<section aria-labelledby="quality-engineering" class="content-panel prose">
    <h2 id="quality-engineering">Quality Engineering and Automation</h2>
    <p data-accomplishment-ids="E01 E02 E03 E06 E08 E12 E50">
        I authored and drove enterprise QA modernization strategies for Global Education, bringing together
        repository-owned testing, shared QA platform capabilities, enterprise end-to-end validation, automated
        quality gates, and objective release governance. I helped shape TAPIR, VISTA, and shift-left quality
        initiatives, positioning TAPIR and VISTA as enterprise confidence layers and working to increase testing
        coverage. I defined end-to-end testing strategies, release-confidence expectations, and business-critical
        testing paths, and led architectural discussions about quality ownership.
    </p>
    <p data-accomplishment-ids="E05 E07 E09 E10 E11">
        I standardized enterprise QA frameworks using Microsoft-, Amazon-, and Google-style maturity models,
        organized TAPIR training and governance, and created shift-left automation frameworks. My implementation
        contributions included directing work involving Playwright, NUnit, QA API, WireMock, and automated testing
        standards. I also created team automation scaffolding and reusable QA templates to support consistent approaches.
    </p>
    <p data-accomplishment-ids="E04">
        These strategies were documented in <cite>E2E Quality Engineering</cite>,
        <cite>Global Ed - QA Automation Overview</cite>, and <cite>Global Ed - QA Automation Roadmap</cite>.
    </p>
</section>

